<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM3-COMPOSITION-DANGLING-REF>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM3-COMPOSITION-DANGLING-REF" ;
  triage:title "run_daemon_with_observability still calls the composition module this same commit deleted" ;
  triage:description "AM.3 deleted crates/atm-daemon/src/composition.rs (790 lines) and its mod composition; declaration, correctly per AM1-RM-003's disposition. However crates/atm-daemon/src/lib.rs:122-126's pub fn run_daemon_with_observability still calls composition::compose_runtime(observability)?.start() -- a dangling reference to the module this same commit removed, left behind instead of being deleted alongside its sole callee. This currently causes no build failure only because crates/atm-daemon/Cargo.toml sets autolib = false with no [lib] table (an AL.8 decision predating AM.3, confirmed via git blame on commit 49ccdfa2), so cargo metadata confirms atm-daemon has exactly one target (a bin from main.rs) and lib.rs plus its entire module tree is excluded from every build/test target. The dead-lib-tree condition itself is pre-existing and separately tracked by the ledger's own AM-PLAN-004 through AM-PLAN-008 items, but this specific dangling reference was newly created by this commit's own edit to lib.rs (removing mod composition; without also removing its sole caller). Independently confirmed by rust-best-practices-agent, ruthless-boundary-qa, arch-qa, req-qa, and rust-qa-agent -- 5 of 6 dispatched reviewers in the same round." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "dead-code" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
